Global Enterprise Human Resources Policies & Guidelines

1. Remote Work & Equipment Policy

1.1 Remote Work Allowance and Stipend

Employees classified as Remote or Hybrid are eligible for a one-time home office setup reimbursement of up to $1,000 USD upon initial hire. Additionally, active remote employees receive a recurring monthly stipend of $150 USD to cover high-speed internet and utility expenses. Receipts must be submitted through the Expense Portal by the 25th of each calendar month.

1.2 Equipment Upgrades and Ownership

Company-issued laptops and hardware remain the sole property of the enterprise and are refreshed every 36 months. Damaged or malfunctioning equipment must be reported to the IT Helpdesk within 24 hours.

2. Paid Time Off (PTO) & Leave Guidelines

2.1 Annual Vacation Accrual

Full-time staff accrue 20 days of paid vacation per calendar year, accruing at a rate of 1.66 days per completed month of service. A maximum of 5 unused PTO days may be carried over into the following calendar year, expiring on March 31st if unspent.

2.2 Parental Leave

All full-time employees with at least 6 months of continuous service are entitled to 16 weeks of 100% paid Parental Leave for the birth, adoption, or foster placement of a child. Parental leave must be taken within the first 12 months following the event.

3. Compensation & Performance Evaluation

3.1 Performance Review Cycles

Formal performance evaluations occur bi-annually in June and December. Merit-based salary adjustments and annual bonus allocations are processed during the Q1 cycle (February effective date) following the end of the fiscal year performance review.

4. Code of Conduct & Workplace Ethics

4.1 Professional Integrity

Employees are required to maintain strict compliance with confidentiality regulations. Unauthorised sharing of enterprise IP or confidential employee data result in immediate disciplinary action up to termination.
